  <file original="src/vs/sessions/contrib/sessionInputBanners/browser/sessionWorktreeCleanupAccessibilityHelp" source-language="en" datatype="plaintext"><body>
    <trans-unit id="sessionWorktreeCleanupHelp.automatic">
      <source xml:lang="en">The Cleanup Settings section can automatically mark merged pull request sessions as done and optionally delete them after a retention period. It also includes a setting to turn the storage cleanup suggestion on or off. Each setting has a Configure in Settings button that opens the Settings editor filtered to that setting.</source>
    </trans-unit>
    <trans-unit id="sessionWorktreeCleanupHelp.cleanup">
      <source xml:lang="en">Activate Clean Up Worktrees to delete the selected sessions' worktrees and mark those sessions as done after confirmation. It is disabled until at least one session is selected, and its label reports how many worktrees will be cleaned up.</source>
    </trans-unit>
    <trans-unit id="sessionWorktreeCleanupHelp.filter">
      <source xml:lang="en">Use the Untouched For selector to choose how long a session must be inactive to be eligible. Changing it re-measures storage and updates the table and summary.</source>
    </trans-unit>
    <trans-unit id="sessionWorktreeCleanupHelp.overview">
      <source xml:lang="en">You are in the Open worktree cleanup editor. It lists agent session worktrees that are inactive and eligible for cleanup so you can reclaim the disk space they use. Cleaning up a session marks it as done and deletes its worktree; you can restore the session later to recreate it.</source>
    </trans-unit>
    <trans-unit id="sessionWorktreeCleanupHelp.reopen">
      <source xml:lang="en">Return to this editor any time by running Open Worktree Cleanup from the Command Palette, the Sessions More Actions menu, or a session's context menu.</source>
    </trans-unit>
    <trans-unit id="sessionWorktreeCleanupHelp.summary">
      <source xml:lang="en">A summary line above the table reports how many worktrees are eligible and about how much storage they use. A nearby info button explains why sessions are included or excluded.</source>
    </trans-unit>
    <trans-unit id="sessionWorktreeCleanupHelp.table">
      <source xml:lang="en">The table lists one row per eligible session with its title, when it was last used, and its worktree size. Use Tab to move into the table. Each row has a checkbox to select it and a session title link that opens the session, and a Select All checkbox in the header toggles every eligible row.</source>
    </trans-unit>
</body></file>
